    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with BUILD SUCCESS. There are only the acceptance test classes in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documenting the fixed table and that it's absent for an unknown region.\n\n2. **`Region.java`** \u2014 Added an IANA `timezone` to each enum constant (NSW\u2192`Australia/Sydney`, VIC\u2192`Australia/Melbourne`, QLD\u2192`Australia/Brisbane`) with a `getTimezone()` accessor, keeping the region-keyed facts in their single home alongside city and postcode.\n\n3. **`TimezoneResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 Mirrors the existing `LocalityResolver`: resolves the locality/region from the owner's customer code, looks it up in `Region`, and returns the IANA timezone (or `null` when the locality carries no known region, leaving the field absent). Kept out of the mapper interface so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit property mapping.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `timezone` mapping expression consistent with the surrounding derived-field mappings.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`, asserting `locality` \"NSW\" \u2192 `timezone` \"Australia/Sydney\") and the full suite are green.",
